  "question": "Given $$A=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 \\\\ -3 & 4\\end{bmatrix},\\quad B=\\begin{bmatrix}5 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 0\\end{bmatrix},$$ verify that $(A+B)^T=A^T+B^T$.",
  "answeroption": "C",
  "explanation": "<b>Addition before transposition</b><br>$$A+B=\\begin{bmatrix}6 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 4\\end{bmatrix}$$<br>Therefore, $$(A+B)^T=\\begin{bmatrix}6 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 4\\end{bmatrix}$$<br><b>Separate transposes</b><br>$$A^T=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -3 \\\\ 2 & 4\\end{bmatrix},\\quad B^T=\\begin{bmatrix}5 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}$$<br>Thus, $$A^T+B^T=\\begin{bmatrix}6 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 4\\end{bmatrix}$$<br>Hence, $(A+B)^T=A^T+B^T$.",
